<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hastings Banda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1898–1997</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hastings Kamuzu Banda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hastings Kamuzu Banda was a Malawian physician and politician who led Nyasaland to independence as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> in 1964. He returned home in 1958 to lead the campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> and was detained during the 1959 emergency. As prime minister and from 1966 president, declared president for life in 1971, he ruled a one-party state until he lost multiparty elections in 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hastings-banda.jpg" alt="Hastings Banda" width="320" height="433" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Archives of Malawi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dr_HK_Banda,_first_president_of_Malawi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
